<article class="env-example" id="0EFM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EFM">Example <span data-tag="0EFM">52.8.6</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/0EFL" data-tag="0EFL">52.8.5</a> we do not know that the inverse systems $H^ i_ J(M/I^ nM)$ satisfy the Mittag-Leffler condition. For example, suppose that $A = \mathbf{Z}_ p[[x, y]]$, $I = (p)$, $J = (p, x)$, and $M = A/(xy - p)$. Then the image of $H^0_ J(M/p^ nM) \to H^0_ J(M/pM)$ is the ideal generated by $y^ n$ in $M/pM = A/(p, xy)$. </p>
</article>